From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 23 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkisp1: commit the MI shadow with the V21 force-update bits

The memory interface latches its buffer base/size from the shadow registers
on a force-update write to CIF_MI_INIT. All variants use SOFT_UPD for this,
and the Rockchip BSP force_cfg_update() writes SOFT_UPD on the rk3566/rk3568
(V21) too, so it must be kept. In addition, on V21 the BSP forces the MP/SP
write shadows by setting ISP21_MP_FORCE_UPD | ISP21_SP_FORCE_UPD on the same
MI_INIT register for the CSI2RX-fed memory interface.

Keep SOFT_UPD on all variants and add the V21 MP/SP force-update bits on V21.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp1/rkisp1-regs.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp1/rkisp1-regs.h
@@ -144,6 +144,9 @@
 /* MI_INIT */
 #define RKISP1_CIF_MI_INIT_SKIP				BIT(2)
 #define RKISP1_CIF_MI_INIT_SOFT_UPD			BIT(4)
+/* rk3566/rk3568 (V21) force-update bits for committing the MI shadow */
+#define RKISP1_CIF_MI_INIT_MP_FORCE_UPD_V21		BIT(20)
+#define RKISP1_CIF_MI_INIT_SP_FORCE_UPD_V21		BIT(21)
 #define RKISP1_CIF_MI_INIT_MP_OUTPUT_YUV400		(0 << 5)
 #define RKISP1_CIF_MI_INIT_MP_OUTPUT_YUV420		(1 << 5)
 #define RKISP1_CIF_MI_INIT_MP_OUTPUT_YUV422		(2 << 5)
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp1/rkisp1-capture.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp1/rkisp1-capture.c
@@ -1044,7 +1044,18 @@
 		else
 			reg = 0;
 
+		/*
+		 * Commit the MI shadow (buffer base/size). Every variant latches
+		 * it with SOFT_UPD - the Rockchip BSP force_cfg_update() writes
+		 * SOFT_UPD on V21 too, so it must stay. On the rk3566/rk3568 (V21)
+		 * the BSP additionally forces the MP/SP write shadows (it sets
+		 * ISP21_MP_FORCE_UPD | ISP21_SP_FORCE_UPD on the same MI_INIT
+		 * register for the CSI2RX-fed memory interface); add those on V21.
+		 */
 		reg |= RKISP1_CIF_MI_INIT_SOFT_UPD;
+		if (rkisp1->info->isp_ver == RKISP1_V21)
+			reg |= RKISP1_CIF_MI_INIT_MP_FORCE_UPD_V21 |
+			       RKISP1_CIF_MI_INIT_SP_FORCE_UPD_V21;
 		rkisp1_write(rkisp1, RKISP1_CIF_MI_INIT, reg);
 
 		rkisp1_set_next_buf(cap);
-- 
